Haakon Studebaker wrote:
> I recently had the pleasure of my monk becoming the Glory of Arioch. He
> received a spellbook of restore ability. Yet he already had a unihorn which
> made me wonder the usefulness of the spell vs. the item.
>
> What does restore ability do that a unihorn can not do?

In my opinion, the potion and spell of restore ability are victims of
Nethack's tendency towards powergaming.  There is no thing they provide
over unicorn horns that can't be made up for simply by being careful of
curses and possibly using a couple extra turns, AND uncorn horns do
other cool things besides: they can be used as quite a good weapon,
they can cure most ill effects including hallucination, and they can
even turn some potions into water or fruit juice, which is also an
identification aid.

The only situation I can think of in which the spell is really more use
than a unicorn horn is if you're being attacked by a mind flayer and
are in danger of sudden brainlessness.  The spell could potentially
always work, while even a blessed unicorn horn has a significant
failure rate over the course of one turn.

